  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sh. Charanjeev Singh S/O Mukhtiar Singh vs Director/Controller on 4 November, 2024 Author: Chief Justice Bench: Chief Justice High Court Of Jammu & Kashmir And Ladakh At Jammu Date:04.11.2024 Wp(C) Pil No.33/2019 1. Sh. Charanjeev Singh S/o Mukhtiar Singh R/o H.No.28, Exchange Road, Jammu. .....Petitioner Through: Mr. Parveen Kapahi, Advocate. versus 1. Director/Controller Drugs & Food Control Organization Muthi. 2. Commissioner Municipality, Municipal Corporation, Jammu. 3. Assistant Director, Food Safety Standard Authority of India Fda Bhawan Kotla Road, New Delhi. .....Respondents Through: Mr. S.S. Nanda, Sr. Aag Mr. Harshwardhan Gupta, Advocate. Coram: Hon'Ble The Chief Justice Hon'Ble Mr. Justice M.A. Chowdhary, Judge Oral Such ice Sh. Charanjeev Singh S/O Mukhtiar Singh vs Director/Controller on 4 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/192523233/ 1 blocks, which come in contact with food products, are generally used for preservation, storage and transportation of perishable food commodities like cheese, meat, fish, chicken etc. However, if, at any stage, the petitioner feels that the said guidelines are being flouted by manufacturers of non-edible ice blocks, he is at liberty to approach this Court again. Whether the order is reportable ? Yes Whether the order is speaking ?",
    "facts": "And, as per the report received from the designated officers, District Jammu and District Kathua, the manufacturers of non-edible ice are adding colour as per the guidelines issued by the FSSAI. Further, a public notice/advisory on edible/non-edible ice as per the guidelines issued by the FSSAI was got published in the Daily Excelsior in its issue dated 14.09.2019 and Greater Kashmir in is issue dated 06.10.2018 for the awareness of the general public including manufacturer of edible/non-edible ice. 5. Though the grievance, as projected by the petitioner, is of grave concern, yet in view of the reports of designated officers of respondent No.1, it seems the concern raised by the petitioner in the present petition has already been addressed as, in view of the said reports, the manufacturers of non-edible ice have been adding colour as per the guidelines issued by the FSSAI so as to distinguish non-edible ice from edible ice.",
    "arguments": "Thus, it is averred that it is the fundamental duty of the State to protect the health and lives of the citizens by taking such legal and stringent measures to prevent the use of contaminated ice blocks as the same cannot be differentiated between edible and non-edible ice for human consumption."
  },
